      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We can rewrite the equation as $\\cos 2x \\cos 3x - \\sin 2x \\sin 3x = 0$.\nUsing the product-to-sum identity, we see that this is equivalent to $\\cos (2x + 3x) = 0$.\nSo, $5x = 90^\\circ + 360^\\circ k$, where $k$ is an integer.\nTherefore, $x = 18^\\circ + 72^\\circ k$.\nThe smallest positive angle is when $k=0$, so $x=18^\\circ$. \nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{18}$.The answer is: 18",
