      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Divide through by $\\cos 2x \\cos 3x$ to obtain:\n$$\\frac{\\sin 2x}{\\cos 2x} = \\frac{\\cos 3x}{\\sin 3x},$$\nor $\\tan 2x = \\cot 3x.$\nThe tangent of an angle is the ratio of the opposite side to the adjacent side in a right triangle, while the cotangent of an angle is the ratio of the adjacent side to the opposite side.\nThus, the situation is as follows:\n[asy]\nunitsize(1 cm);\n\npair A;\n\ndraw((-1,0)--(1,0));\nfor (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i) {\n    draw(A+dir(10 * i) -- A+dir(10 * (i + 1)), Arrow);\n}\n\ndot((0.71, 0));\ndot((0.63, 0));\ndot((0.78, 0));\ndot((0.55, 0));\ndot((0.94, 0));\nlabel(\"$2x$\", A+dir(20), NE);\nlabel(\"3x\", A+dir(90), SE);\n[/asy]\nThe corresponding angles in the diagram correspond to the given equation of the ratio of two tangents/cotangents.\nTherefore, the problem is split into two cases:\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(1 cm);\n\npair A, B;\n\ndraw((-1,0)--(1,0));\nfor (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i) {\n    draw(A+dir(10 * i) -- A+dir(10 * (i + 1)), Arrow);\n}\n\ndot((0.71, 0));\ndot((0.63, 0));\ndot((0.78, 0));\ndot((0.55, 0));\ndot((0.94, 0));\ndot(Weekendscboomer's(a), A+dir(20), NE);\nlabel(\"$2x$\", A+dir(20), NE);\nlabel(\"3x\", Weekendschibstagboomer's(a), SE);\n[/asy]\nCase 1 (Figure 1)\n[asy]\nunitsize(1 cm);\n\npair A, B, HourHand;\n\nDraw(A+dir(176.5)--A+dir(183.5)--A+dir(190.5), Arrow);\nDraw((A+dir(176.5)--A+dir(183.5)--A+dir(190.5))--(A+dir(230)--A+dir(237)--A+dir(244)));\nDraw(A+dir(20)--A+dir(90)--A+dir(160), Arrow);\n\ndot((A+dir(90)--(A+dir(176.5)-A+dir(20), 1));\nlabel(\"$2x$\", (A+dir(90)--(A+dir(176.5)-A+dir(20), 1), S);\nlabel(\"$3x$\", (A+dir(237)--A+dir(244)--(A+dir(20)--A+dir(90), 1), se;\n\ndraw((-1,0)--(1,0));\nfor (int i = 0; i < 12; ++i) {\n    draw(A+dir(10 * i) -- A+dir(10 * (i + 1)), Arrow);\n}\n\nA = intersectionpoint((1,0)--(A+dir(176.5)--A+dir(183.5)--A+dir(190.5)), (1.5,0)--(H.HourHand--H+.H.H./2*1.E(-1)--H+,1));\ndraw((A+dir(20)+A+dir(90)--(A+dir(176.5)-A+dir(20), 1)--HourHand, Arrow);\n\nlabel(\"$2x$\", A+dir(20), NE);\nlabel(\"3x\", Weekendschibstagboomer's(a), SE);\nlabel(\"dst.\", H+dir(3), N);\n\nlabel(r\"$2x$\", A.HourHand/6+d(A!H.S.centralAngle(Seconds)/(12*Minutes)));\nlabel(r\"$3x$\", H+dir(20), NE);\nlabel(r\"d\", Weekendscboomer's(a), S);\nlabel(r\"$a$\", H+.Shelladding([centralAngle(20) / (12*60)]*1.E(-1), direction(90), SE);\nlabel(r\"$b$\", H+.Shelladding([centralAngle(42) / (12*60)]*1.E(-1), direction(90), SE;\n\nHomework Help | MathNew Users | Jerry Benson | Math Tutorials | Mr. B. Math Carnival | Mr. Benson | Mr.B I am not alone\n\nPLACE ORDER RIGHT AWAY",
